/*
Original work, written for tests/fixtures/nonlinear-timeline (temporal-
consistency mechanism material, 2026-08-03). Parallel-action structure:
a heist crosscut between two threads using MEANWHILE / SIMULTANEOUSLY
heading markers, per the markers extractTemporalConstraints() actually
parses (checked against heading + extracted narrative fields). Temporally
clean as written -- 0 expected contradictions.
*/

INT. MERIDIAN MUSEUM - EAST GALLERY - NIGHT

Security lights hum on standby. LUCA REYES, thirties, in a maintenance jumpsuit, kneels at a display case, feeding a thin blade under the glass seal.

LUCA
(into an earpiece)
I'm at the case. Tell me the loop's still holding.

INT. VAN - PARKED ACROSS THE STREET - NIGHT - MEANWHILE

MEANWHILE, at the curb: PRIYA OSEI, forties, surrounded by monitors, watches a looped feed of an empty gallery.

PRIYA
(into headset)
Loop's holding. You've got six minutes before the guard's actual round catches up to the fake one.

INT. MERIDIAN MUSEUM - EAST GALLERY - NIGHT

Luca lifts the case lid an inch, freezes as a servo whines somewhere in the ceiling.

LUCA
Something just moved. Camera or vent?

PRIYA (V.O.)
(over earpiece)
Vent. Building's just breathing. Keep going.

INT. MERIDIAN MUSEUM - SERVICE CORRIDOR - NIGHT - SIMULTANEOUSLY

SIMULTANEOUSLY, down a service corridor: DESMOND OKAFOR, twenties, disables a keypad panel with a cloned fob, sweat beading at his temple.

DESMOND
(muttering to himself)
Third try's the charm. Third try's the charm.

The panel clicks green. He exhales, pushes through the door.

INT. MERIDIAN MUSEUM - EAST GALLERY - NIGHT

Luca eases the artifact -- a small gold reliquary -- free of its mount, wraps it, tucks it against his chest.

LUCA
(into earpiece)
Got it. Moving to the corridor now.

INT. VAN - PARKED ACROSS THE STREET - NIGHT - MEANWHILE

MEANWHILE, Priya's monitor flickers -- the loop stutters, one frame repeating.

PRIYA
(sharp)
Loop's degrading. Someone's running a diagnostic on the feed. Move faster than fast.

INT. MERIDIAN MUSEUM - SERVICE CORRIDOR - NIGHT

Desmond reaches a junction, checks both directions, waves Luca in as he arrives from the gallery.

DESMOND
Priya says we're bleeding time.

LUCA
Priya's always right about that. Which door.

INT. MERIDIAN MUSEUM - LOADING DOCK - NIGHT

The two of them reach a rolling door, Desmond already working the manual release.

DESMOND
Thirty seconds and we're a delivery van nobody remembers seeing.

The door grinds up. Night air floods in.

INT. VAN - PARKED ACROSS THE STREET - NIGHT - SIMULTANEOUSLY

SIMULTANEOUSLY, Priya's monitors go fully dark, replaced by a live security override banner.

PRIYA
(into headset, urgent)
Loop's dead. They're on live feed. However far you are from that door, be further.

EXT. MERIDIAN MUSEUM - LOADING DOCK - NIGHT

Luca and Desmond burst out into the alley just as a spotlight sweeps the far wall behind them.

LUCA
(running)
Define "further."

DESMOND
(running)
The van, ideally.

EXT. ALLEY BEHIND MUSEUM - NIGHT

They round the corner at a dead sprint. The van's side door is already open, engine running.

INT. VAN - MOVING - NIGHT

Luca and Desmond pile in. Priya floors it before the door fully shuts, the reliquary clutched safe in Luca's lap.

PRIYA
Anyone want to explain the vent noise before I have a heart attack retroactively?

LUCA
(catching his breath)
Building. Breathing.

The van swings hard onto the main road, sirens rising somewhere behind them, still distant.
